{
  "case_id": "2008-08-295",
  "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Travelers Indemnity Company)",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In 1988, the Second Circuit decided in two separate decisions that a bankruptcy court exercising its core jurisdiction had properly confirmed the plan of reorganization that resolved present and future claims against Johns-Manville and the insurers who funded Manville's reorganization plan."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At the time of the 1986 order, had these independent actions started? I thought at the time of the 1986 order the concerns were suits involving Manville's liability and the insurers' derivative obligation to cover."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Travelers Indemnity Company)",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The bankruptcy court judge, interpreting his own order, explicitly held that the 1986 order was intended and was always intended to enjoin direct actions against Travelers based upon, arising out of, or relating to the insurance policies Manville purchased from Travelers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: How did they get the notice? You say it's broad notice. What exactly was done?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How can it be successive when they didn't even get their -- I mean they -- these people haven't had a day in court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ostrager",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OSTRAGER: There was broad notice to the people who would be affected by the issuance of the injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But, putting aside questions of notice, if these parties had been represented in the appeal of the 1986 order, maybe the subject matter jurisdiction ruling was correct; maybe it was incorrect; but it's done."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I don't think there's a notice question. I thought there were 5,538 plaintiffs here and -- that you represent, and every one of them has already gotten money from the trust except for two who have filed claims against it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Issacharoff",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ISSACHAROFF: I agree that that is the general rule, that is correct. I agree further that the Second Circuit expressly held at page 31a that the error of the bankruptcy court was that it subsequently interpreted the order more broadly than the Second Circuit had affirmed in 1988."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, why not -- because there is a good constitutional protection; it's called the due process clause. If the bankruptcy judge goes too far, it's a due process violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is it not the case that most of the claims are claims based on -- based on Manville?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-08-295",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "450ddbf1613a9a80048b569c47739714bdda54d85cf837344883b5a49d6adcbe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-450ddbf1613a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COHN: So, getting back to the next point I would like to make is, as Mr. Issacharoff has stated, the Second Circuit was presented and the bankruptcy court was presented in 1986 with a plan and with an order that was stated to be premised upon the derivative liability of Travelers for Manville."
    },
